# netsurf: Request gets a body to read -- text, json, formData,
# arrayBuffer, blob, bytes, body, bodyUsed, clone (patch 259)
# Generated 2026-10-12
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 258)
#
# The bridge's Request (macsurf_qjs.c) stored init.body as it was given
# and had no readers: req.text(), req.json(), req.formData() ... were not
# functions, `body` was the raw value rather than a stream, bodyUsed never
# changed, and the URL was not resolved. vita_polyfill.js now replaces it
# with a Request that shares Response's body machinery (extractBody, _take
# and the readers, patches 132 / 256-258), following Chromium (checked
# case by case):
#
#  - the URL resolved against the document; DELETE GET HEAD OPTIONS POST
#    PUT upper-cased, other methods kept; a GET / HEAD with a body throws;
#  - `body` a ReadableStream or null; the body's Content-Type unless one is
#    set (text/plain;charset=UTF-8, multipart with its boundary,
#    url-encoded; bytes get none);
#  - new Request(req) takes req's body and marks req used -- even when
#    init gives another body -- and a used Request cannot be wrapped,
#    cloned, read again or fetched; clone() tees a streamed body;
#  - fetch(req) sends req's own body (not re-extracted from the stream)
#    and uses it up;
#  - every field a prototype getter (no own properties), signal an
#    AbortSignal, destination "", keepalive false.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-fetch-body.html checks 23-30, 30/30 over http
# and https (Chromium 30/30; run 35's build stops at check 25, "not a
# function").
